A||||10||fotofrank||Broken Rearview mirror||||11||
Z||000000||fotofrank||12-18-2000||01:17 PM||||Yes I have a red face. The mirror broke off and I glued the metal piece back on . I used commercial glue for this but I glued the metal pice on backwards. How od I get it off without breaking the windshield?<P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://fotofrank.homestead.com/foto1~ns4.html||||reg||11
Z||000001||deceler8||12-18-2000||02:01 PM||||Try using a razor blade.<P>When you glue the piece back on again, use clear silicone (or any silicone, for that matter).<P>I've never had luck using the rear view mirror adhesive. Silicone, on the other hand, has worked and held for years.<P>And any color will do...you won't see it. And silicone will hold the piece in place while it cures...also allows repositioning and easy removal.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||12-18-2000||03:17 PM||||I asked a glass place that very ques. awhile back and basicly he said "Good Luck" he uses a torch with GREAT care.||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||12-18-2000||03:50 PM||||Another option you have if you can't get the piece off is to glue another mirror mounting button to the upside down one and attach the mirror to that.<P>It's possible this will work without the "oops" even showing once the mirror is on.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||12-18-2000||05:26 PM||||haha torch,  no way I'd ever use that!<P>I know that the glue is some pretty tough stuff, but maybe there is some kind of solvent that would work, as long as you didnt drip any on the dash.  I would think that the glue is some sort of cynocyanide type (super glue is in this class of glues), so possibly some super glue remover.  ACE hardwares in your are should carry it.  If not that, just try a bunch of solvents and a razor blade.<P>Take your time, haste makes waste!<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Stoic||12-18-2000||05:46 PM||||I don't know how strong the glue is, but sometimes you can get lucky with a hair dryer<P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||12-18-2000||09:10 PM||||<I>exactly</I> what kind of glue did you use. It makes a diferance.......||||reg||1
Z||000007||fotofrank||12-19-2000||07:02 PM||||Thanks for the ideas guys and gals. During my snow drive home last night (2 hours) I had plenty of time to "worry" the button with my pocketknife. I picked one edge and kept working it till I got thr edge of the blade under it. It then just popped off. Thanks again... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Peace and Happiness<BR>Frank and his fotoflash, an '84 SE 2M4<BR>http://fotofrank.homestead.com/foto1~ns4.html||||reg||10
